  "idea": "Zapier vs Make.com: price comparison and complex scenario limits",
  "text": "Why Zapier's task-based pricing will drain your budget once you scale past ten thousand runs. Every filter check, formatter step, and webhook trigger burns an individual paid task credit. A single customer onboarding flow can eat eight tasks, quickly costing hundreds of dollars monthly. Make solves this by processing bulk arrays and iterative data within single operations for pennies. You protect profit margins while scaling transaction volume seamlessly.",
